IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II -- THE CONTRIBUTORY PERIODS (sections 49 to 49.2) AND THE TOTALS OF
-- PENSIONABLE EARNINGS (sections 50 to 50.2).
--
-- The contributory period is a run of months from the 18th birthday (or 1966) to the earliest of a
-- set of ending events, less months excluded. The first additional and second additional
-- contributory periods run on from 2019 and 2024 and have no exclusions. The totals add up the
-- pensionable earnings of each month of the period (sections 51 to 51.3, cp3-pensionable-earnings.l4).
--
-- A month is the DATE of its first day. Ages go through section 2(2) of the Act: "reaches 18" is the
-- first day of the month after the 18th birthday's month, and a period "ending with the time when he
-- reached" an age includes the month of the birthday (section 2(2)(a)). "The month preceding the month in
-- which he reaches 70" is therefore the month of the 70th birthday.

§ `Part II -- Division B -- contributory periods and totals (sections 49 to 50.2)`

§§ `Helpers of this module (no provision licenses them)`

-- Not a provision: the number of months from one month to another, both included; zero if the second is earlier.
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the number of months from one month to another, both included` first last MEANS
    max 0 ((`the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` first last) PLUS 1)

-- Not a provision: the earlier of two months.
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cp3 — the earlier of two dates` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- Not a provision: the later of two months.
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cp3 — the later of two dates` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `49 -- the contributory period`

-- src:1148 | 49 The contributory period of a contributor is the period commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and ending
@ref Act s 49 (src:1148)
`s 49 — the first day of 1966, the earliest start of the contributory period` MEANS YMD 1966 1 1

-- src:1148 | 49 The contributory period of a contributor is the period commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and ending
@ref Act s 49 (src:1148)
GIVEN `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: the contributory period starts on 1 January 1966 or when the contributor reaches 18,
-- whichever is the later. Reaching 18 is the first day of the month after the 18th birthday's month
-- (section 2(2)), and the period starts with that month.
`s 49 — the first month of the contributory period` `the contributor's date of birth` MEANS
    `cp3 — the later of two dates` `s 49 — the first day of 1966, the earliest start of the contributory period` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 18)

-- src:1149 | (a) where a benefit other than a disability pension commences before the end of 1986, when he reaches sixty-five years of age, or if he makes a contribution for earnings after he reaches sixty-five years of age, with the month for which he last made such a contribution, and in any case not later than the month in which he dies, or
@ref Act s 49(a) (src:1149)
GIVEN `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month for which the contributor last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65, if the contributor made one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: for a benefit other than a disability pension that commences before the end of 1986,
-- the period ends when the contributor reaches 65 (the month of the 65th birthday is included), or,
-- if the contributor made a contribution for earnings after 65, with the month of the last such
-- contribution, and in any case not later than the month in which the contributor dies.
`s 49(a) — the last month of the contributory period, for a benefit other than a disability pension that commences before the end of 1986` `the contributor's date of birth` `the month for which the contributor last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65, if the contributor made one` `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the month the period would end`
    WHEN JUST died THEN `cp3 — the earlier of two dates` `the month the period would end` (`the month of a date` died)
    WHERE
        `the month of the 65th birthday` MEANS `the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 65)
        `the month the period would end` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the month for which the contributor last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65, if the contributor made one`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the month of the 65th birthday`
            WHEN JUST last THEN `the month of a date` last

-- src:1150 | (b) where a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit commences after the end of 1986, with the earliest of
-- src:1151 | (i) the month preceding the month in which he reaches seventy years of age,
-- src:1152 | (ii) the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1153 | (iii) the month preceding the month in which the retirement pension commences,
@ref Act s 49(b) (src:1150-1153)
GIVEN `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: for a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit
-- that commences after the end of 1986, the period ends with the earliest of (i) the month before the
-- month in which the contributor reaches 70, (ii) the month in which the contributor dies and (iii)
-- the month before the month in which the retirement pension commences.
`s 49(b) — the last month of the contributory period, for a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit that commences after the end of 1986` `the contributor's date of birth` `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does` MEANS
    `cp3 — the earlier of two dates` (`cp3 — the earlier of two dates` `limb (i)` `limb (ii)`) `limb (iii)`
    WHERE
        `limb (i)` MEANS `add months` (`the month following the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 70)) (0 MINUS 1) 
        `limb (ii)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `limb (i)`
            WHEN JUST died THEN `the month of a date` died
        `limb (iii)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `limb (i)`
            WHEN JUST started THEN `add months` (`the month of a date` started) (0 MINUS 1)

-- src:1149 | (a) where a benefit other than a disability pension commences before the end of 1986, when he reaches sixty-five years of age, or if he makes a contribution for earnings after he reaches sixty-five years of age, with the month for which he last made such a contribution, and in any case not later than the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1150 | (b) where a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit commences after the end of 1986, with the earliest of
-- src:1151 | (i) the month preceding the month in which he reaches seventy years of age,
-- src:1152 | (ii) the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1153 | (iii) the month preceding the month in which the retirement pension commences,
@ref Act s 49(a), (b) (src:1149-1153)
`s 49(a), (b) — the first day of 1987, the end of 1986 having passed` MEANS YMD 1987 1 1

-- src:1149 | (a) where a benefit other than a disability pension commences before the end of 1986, when he reaches sixty-five years of age, or if he makes a contribution for earnings after he reaches sixty-five years of age, with the month for which he last made such a contribution, and in any case not later than the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1150 | (b) where a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit commences after the end of 1986, with the earliest of
-- src:1151 | (i) the month preceding the month in which he reaches seventy years of age,
-- src:1152 | (ii) the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1153 | (iii) the month preceding the month in which the retirement pension commences,
@ref Act s 49(a), (b) (src:1149-1153)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the month with which the benefit commences` IS A DATE
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month for which the contributor last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65, if the contributor made one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
-- Plain gloss: which ending applies depends on the benefit and when it commences: paragraph (a) for a
-- benefit other than a disability pension that commences before the end of 1986, paragraph (b) for a
-- benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit that commences after
-- it. NOTHING means section 49 gives no end for the benefit (a disability pension, or a
-- post-retirement disability benefit after 1986): the minimum qualifying period of section 44 and
-- the rules of Division C give those their own periods.
`s 49 — the last month of the contributory period for a benefit` kind `the month with which the benefit commences` `the contributor's date of birth` `the month for which the contributor last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65, if the contributor made one` `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does` MEANS
    BRANCH IF kind EQUALS `a disability pension` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the month with which the benefit commences` LESS THAN `s 49(a), (b) — the first day of 1987, the end of 1986 having passed`
                THEN JUST (`s 49(a) — the last month of the contributory period, for a benefit other than a disability pension that commences before the end of 1986` `the contributor's date of birth` `the month for which the contributor last made a contribution for earnings after reaching 65, if the contributor made one` `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died`)
           IF kind EQUALS `a post-retirement disability benefit` THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`s 49(b) — the last month of the contributory period, for a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit that commences after the end of 1986` `the contributor's date of birth` `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does`)

-- src:1154 | but excluding
-- src:1155 | (c) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1156 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 49(c), (d) (src:1154-1156)
`s 49(d) — the first day of 1978, December 1977 having passed` MEANS YMD 1978 1 1

-- src:1154 | but excluding
-- src:1155 | (c) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1156 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 49(c), (d) (src:1154-1156)
GIVEN `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month for which the benefit is payable` IS A DATE
      `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a month is left out of the contributory period if it was excluded for disability, or
-- if, for a benefit payable for a month after December 1977, the contributor was a family allowance
-- recipient in it and the year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the
-- basic exemption for the year.
-- out of range: provincial pension plans (not among the inputs): a month excluded by reason of disability under a provincial pension plan is taken as a fact.
`s 49(c), (d) — a month is excluded from the contributory period` `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` `the month for which the benefit is payable` `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month` `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month` MEANS
        `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`
    OR  (    `the month for which the benefit is payable` AT LEAST `s 49(d) — the first day of 1978, December 1977 having passed`
         AND `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month`
         AND `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` AT MOST `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month`)

-- src:1147 | Contributory period
-- src:1148 | 49 The contributory period of a contributor is the period commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and ending
-- src:1149 | (a) where a benefit other than a disability pension commences before the end of 1986, when he reaches sixty-five years of age, or if he makes a contribution for earnings after he reaches sixty-five years of age, with the month for which he last made such a contribution, and in any case not later than the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1150 | (b) where a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit commences after the end of 1986, with the earliest of
-- src:1151 | (i) the month preceding the month in which he reaches seventy years of age,
-- src:1152 | (ii) the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1153 | (iii) the month preceding the month in which the retirement pension commences,
-- src:1154 | but excluding
-- src:1155 | (c) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1156 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 49 (src:1147-1156)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
      `the month is excluded under paragraph (c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a month is in the contributory period if it is between the first month and the last
-- month (both included) and is not excluded.
`s 49 — a month is in the contributory period` month first last `the month is excluded under paragraph (c) or (d)` MEANS
        `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `the month of a date` first
    AND `the month of a date` month AT MOST `the month of a date` last
    AND (NOT `the month is excluded under paragraph (c) or (d)`)

-- src:1147 | Contributory period
-- src:1148 | 49 The contributory period of a contributor is the period commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and ending
-- src:1149 | (a) where a benefit other than a disability pension commences before the end of 1986, when he reaches sixty-five years of age, or if he makes a contribution for earnings after he reaches sixty-five years of age, with the month for which he last made such a contribution, and in any case not later than the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1150 | (b) where a benefit other than a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit commences after the end of 1986, with the earliest of
-- src:1151 | (i) the month preceding the month in which he reaches seventy years of age,
-- src:1152 | (ii) the month in which he dies, or
-- src:1153 | (iii) the month preceding the month in which the retirement pension commences,
-- src:1154 | but excluding
-- src:1155 | (c) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1156 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 49 (src:1147-1156)
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
      `the number of months from the first to the last that are excluded under paragraph (c) or (d)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the number of months in the contributory period is the months from the first month to
-- the last (both included), less the months excluded.
`s 49 — the number of months in the contributory period` first last `the number of months from the first to the last that are excluded under paragraph (c) or (d)` MEANS
    max 0 ((`cp3 — the number of months from one month to another, both included` first last) MINUS `the number of months from the first to the last that are excluded under paragraph (c) or (d)`)

§§ `49.1 and 49.2 -- the first and the second additional contributory period`

-- Not a provision: sections 49.1 and 49.2 end the additional contributory period the same way: the
-- earliest of the month before the 70th birthday's month is reached, the month of death, and the month
-- before the retirement pension commences.
GIVEN `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cp3 — the last month of an additional contributory period` `the contributor's date of birth` `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died` `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does` MEANS
    `cp3 — the earlier of two dates` (`cp3 — the earlier of two dates` `limb (a)` `limb (b)`) `limb (c)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS `add months` (`the month following the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 70)) (0 MINUS 1)
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the month in which the contributor dies, if the contributor has died`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `limb (a)`
            WHEN JUST died THEN `the month of a date` died
        `limb (c)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the month with which the retirement pension commences, if it does`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `limb (a)`
            WHEN JUST started THEN `add months` (`the month of a date` started) (0 MINUS 1)

